  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual and reproductive health of girls and women with intellectual disabilities - phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address the sexual and reproductive health issues faced by girls and women with intellectual disabilities in Georgia. Building on previous work in Tbilisi, Gori, and Rustavi, the project will expand to Batumi, Adjara. 
These women and their families struggle with inadequate healthcare services, lack of appropriate sexual education, and societal stigmatization. 
The project will replicate successful activities from the previous locations and introduce new initiatives to improve healthcare access, provide comprehensive sexual education, and combat stigmatization. By engaging community leaders, healthcare professionals, and families, the project aims to create a supportive environment that promotes the health and well-being of girls and women with intellectual disabilities.
Additional trainings for families will be held in Tbilisi, Gori and Rustavi and two awareness-raising fairs will be organised.</narrative>
  </description>
